{"title":"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of positive integers with only odd digits satisfying the following condition: any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/4045d6bc2de65aea75286ad613b46fa5a699559d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> digits must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> smallest elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Find the remainder upon dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We construct the elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> digit by digit from right to left. Let a valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit number in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. To form a valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cb3f3a8b3bbfc702c5863d16602a06cded535d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />-digit number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" />, we prepend an odd digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/2006ca776f2a0b6dd5dbd77653b42a5d9c90982a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d \\in \\{1, 3, 5, 7, 9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e3f65a81bbba44599d1c9e365fa691df687326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} = d \\cdot 10^n + x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c134ae9d194442eec9a0584ff74fc944ce9251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{n+1}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is already divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b37580db89fddff13088a04467e5876a35422710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n = k \\cdot 5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Substituting this in gives: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a4538bae02fb01a72c96892c036cc1f9a3dcaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{n+1} = d \\cdot 2^n \\cdot 5^n + k \\cdot 5^n = 5^n (d \\cdot 2^n + k)\\]\" width=\"323\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> to be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c134ae9d194442eec9a0584ff74fc944ce9251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{n+1}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />, the term inside the parenthesis must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eb7c9ccec4f2e57600884620e5d7fb953ea9ee3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d \\cdot 2^n + k \\equiv 0 \\pmod 5 \\implies d \\cdot 2^n \\equiv -k \\pmod 5\\]\" width=\"407\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/a/09a358c10b20dd7c82540bb9a0dfecacda0b7261.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(2^n, 5) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />, this linear congruence has a unique solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Because the set of allowed odd digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f1eab6a674efc2895a271c337e80a77811ebcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 3, 5, 7, 9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> forms a complete residue system modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there is exactly one unique odd digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfies the condition for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Thus, there is exactly one valid element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> for each digit length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Constructing the first few unique elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />: \n</p>\n<pre>  item <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n  item <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e4c2930d79c57bee209557767b878cd704ea46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n  item <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/531204a6ace18de0514d0adfd920358e6d0c2e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$375$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />\n  item <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/0/df09e354888b6ce4f2cea4c5d2d5aedee6052627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9375$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />\n  item <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a95ea88d86d76000ff31f715ecffd60fe95fc56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$59375$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />\n</pre>\n<p><br />\nWe want to find the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> smallest elements, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffae46690a0da1e35b4025cedd6b529eafbee6ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\sum_{i=1}^{20} x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"84\" height=\"55\" />, modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that for any term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/2517ce15b7189285d40592f59ae313e758b1f42e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, the number is formed by adding place values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904f9084f42eb25076a2c9c06d7fb8e402fea693.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> or greater to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/531204a6ace18de0514d0adfd920358e6d0c2e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$375$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/2517ce15b7189285d40592f59ae313e758b1f42e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a61acd75917d487c7809a9f5c55a6f401289dc71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_i \\equiv 375 \\pmod{1000}\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>There is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> term ending in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> term ending in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e4c2930d79c57bee209557767b878cd704ea46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms that are congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/daed64f7f656bc6f0a0c5ab503e0b690f473b83f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$375 \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />. Summing these together: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/6651f692781ee03d59d7c07dbbf77f0c01a86741.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A \\equiv 5 + 75 + 18 \\times 375 \\pmod{1000}\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/0422e93a9c51d6c86bb67b811659df0406c952fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A \\equiv 80 + 6750 \\pmod{1000}\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/858a8d90e06421e266f846e313285bf93a4e381f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A \\equiv 6830 \\pmod{1000} \\equiv 830\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<pre>~Asmit(curiously_dumb)\n</pre>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006\">Mock AIME 5 2005-2006</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=76847\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018040443\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 405/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1445/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 203/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11763/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.418      1 Template:Mock_AIME_box\n100.00%    7.418      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13378:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018040443 and revision id 290830. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}